    {
      "name": "remote logout",
      "usage": "k2 remote logout --host HOST [--token-stdin]",
      "description": "End this computer's session on HOST (POST /cli/auth/logout, the token in an Authorization header). The token is the one k2 talk <ws>@HOST sends ($K2_REMOTE_TOKEN, connect-tokens.json, then the keychain) or one read from stdin; never on the command line. After HOST answers, the saved copies of that token for HOST are removed (connect-tokens.json and the keychain); a saved token that differs is kept. It can't revoke an owner token (a restart of that server's daemon does), and success can't prove a session existed: the server answers 200 either way. Exit: 0 signed out, 1 no answer or an unexpected one, 2 usage, 3 HOST refused (nothing removed).",
      "args": [],
      "flags": [
        {"name": "--host", "arg": "HOST", "description": "The server: a name (https) or a URL; plain http:// only to this computer. Required."},
        {"name": "--token-stdin", "arg": null, "description": "Read the token from stdin instead of the saved one."}
      ]
    },
